/-!
# Complements on `AdjoinRoot`

Mathlib's `AdjoinRoot.map` sends a ring homomorphism `f : R →+* S`, together with a divisibility
`q ∣ p.map f`, to a ring homomorphism `AdjoinRoot p →+* AdjoinRoot q`. It records the action on
`AdjoinRoot.of` and on `AdjoinRoot.root` (`map_of`, `map_root`) but not the action on the class of
a general polynomial, and says nothing about surjectivity. Both are added here, together with the
description of the `R`-linear endomorphisms of `AdjoinRoot g`, for any `g`, that commute with
multiplication by the root, and the annihilators of the powers of the root in the truncated
polynomial ring `R[X]/(X ^ n)`. It also adds the algebra maps out of `AdjoinRoot f` into any
algebra, the `n`th-root classes in `R[X]/(X ^ n - C a)`, the degree-bounded representatives of
classes modulo a monic relator, rank counts for quotients of `R[X]/(X ^ n)`, and the base change
of `AdjoinRoot g`, in particular of the truncated polynomial algebra `k[X]/(X ^ N)`.

## Main results

* `AdjoinRoot.map_mk`: the map sends the class of `x` to the class of `x.map f`. Mathlib states
  this only in the specialised form `WeierstrassCurve.Affine.CoordinateRing.map_mk`. Marked
  `@[simp]`, like its neighbours `AdjoinRoot.map_of` and `AdjoinRoot.map_root`.
* `AdjoinRoot.map_surjective`: the map is surjective when `f` is.
* `AdjoinRoot.ker_mk`: the kernel of `AdjoinRoot.mk p` is the ideal generated by `p`.
* `AdjoinRoot.ker_map_map_of_surjective`: for surjective `f`, the kernel of
  `AdjoinRoot p → AdjoinRoot (p.map f)` is the extension of the kernel of `f`, so that
  `AdjoinRoot (p.map f)` is the reduction of `AdjoinRoot p` modulo `ker f`.
* `AdjoinRoot.algHomOfDvd_mk`: for `g ∣ f`, the reduction `AdjoinRoot f →ₐ[R] AdjoinRoot g` sends
  the class of `p` to the class of `p`; `AdjoinRoot.algHomOfDvd_algHomOfDvd` and
  `AdjoinRoot.algHomOfDvd_self`: these reductions compose, and reduction modulo `f` itself is the
  identity.
* `AdjoinRoot.algHom_mk`: an algebra map out of `AdjoinRoot g` sends the class of `p` to the
  evaluation of `p` at the image of the root.
* `AdjoinRoot.algHomEquiv`: over any commutative ring, the algebra maps out of `AdjoinRoot f`
  into any algebra, commutative or not, are the roots of `f`. Mathlib's `AdjoinRoot.equiv` is the
  version over a field with values in a domain.
* `AdjoinRoot.root_X_pow_sub_one_pow`: the class of `X` in `R[X]/(X ^ n - 1)` is an `n`th root of
  unity.
* `AdjoinRoot.root_X_pow_sub_C_pow`: the class of `X` in `R[X]/(X ^ n - C a)` is an `n`th root
  of `a`, over any commutative ring. Mathlib states this only over a field.
* `AdjoinRoot.isUnit_root_X_pow_sub_C`: that root is a unit when `a` is a unit and `n ≠ 0`.
* `AdjoinRoot.isUnit_mk_iff_isCoprime`: the class of `g` is a unit of `AdjoinRoot f` exactly when
  `f` and `g` are coprime.
* `AdjoinRoot.exists_of_pow_mul_eq_of_C_mul_X_sub_C`: for any `a, g ∈ R`, a power of `a` carries
  every element of `R[X]/(aX - g)` to the class of a constant, since `aX = g` there.
* `AdjoinRoot.isUnit_mk_mul_sub_iff_isCoprime`: modulo a product `p * q`, the class of `p - q` is
  a unit exactly when `p` and `q` are coprime.
* `AdjoinRoot.mk_modByMonic`: for any relator, a polynomial and its remainder have the same
  class.
* `AdjoinRoot.exists_degree_lt_mk_eq`, `AdjoinRoot.mk_eq_mk_iff_of_degree_lt`: for a monic
  relator, every class is represented by a polynomial of degree less than that of the relator, and
  that representative is unique. Mathlib records the same content as `AdjoinRoot.modByMonicHom`
  (the class of `p` goes to `p %ₘ g`), a right inverse of `AdjoinRoot.mk`
  (`AdjoinRoot.mk_leftInverse`), and as the power basis `AdjoinRoot.powerBasis'`; these two lemmas
  are the formulation in terms of degrees.
* `AdjoinRoot.eq_mulRight_of_root_mul`: an `R`-linear endomorphism of `AdjoinRoot g`
  that commutes with multiplication by the root is multiplication by its value at `1`. The
  characterization holds for any relator `g`.
* `AdjoinRoot.algebraTensorAlgEquiv`: the base change `T ⊗[R] R[X]/(g)` of `AdjoinRoot g` to an
  `R`-algebra `T` is `T[X]/(g)`, with `g` mapped into `T[X]`. Mathlib's `AdjoinRoot.tensorAlgEquiv`
  lands in `AdjoinRoot` over `T ⊗[R] R` instead; this is it followed by `T ⊗[R] R ≃ T`, the form
  in which norms over `T` of base changes of `AdjoinRoot g` can be computed.
* `AdjoinRoot.free_X_pow`, `AdjoinRoot.finite_X_pow`: the truncated polynomial algebra
  `R[X]/(X ^ N)` is a finite free `R`-module.
* `AdjoinRoot.tensorXPowAlgEquiv k R N`: for a `k`-algebra `R`, the `k`-algebra isomorphism
  `k[X]/(X ^ N) ⊗[k] R ≃ R[X]/(X ^ N)`, natural in `R` (`AdjoinRoot.tensorXPowAlgEquiv_comp_map`).
* `AdjoinRoot.root_X_pow_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff`: in the truncated polynomial ring `R[X]/(X ^ n)`,
  the annihilator of `x ^ i` is generated by `x ^ (n - i)`, where `x` is the root, for every `i`
  (for `i > n` both sides hold because `x ^ i = 0` and `n - i = 0`);
  `AdjoinRoot.root_X_pow_pow_sub_mul_eq_zero_iff` is the same statement with `i` and `n - i`
  exchanged.
* `AdjoinRoot.finrank_quotient_span_root_X_pow_pow`: for `p ≤ n` and `R` nontrivial, the
  quotient of `R[X]/(X ^ n)` by `x ^ p` has rank `p`.
* `AdjoinRoot.finrank_quotient_span_op_root_X_pow_pow`,
  `AdjoinRoot.finrank_quotient_map_mkQ_span_op_root_X_pow_pow`: the same count for the cyclic
  right modules `M_j`, the quotients of the opposite ring by `op (x ^ j)`, and the quotient of
  `M_j` by the image of `x ^ m`, which has rank `min j m`.
* `RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular.isSMulRegular_adjoinRoot_C_mul_X_sub_C`: for a weakly
  regular sequence `a, g` on `R`, multiplication by `a` is injective on `R[X]/(aX - g)`.
* `Polynomial.quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot`, `Polynomial.quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot`: the cyclic
  polynomial quotient as an `R`-module and as an `R`-algebra is `AdjoinRoot f`; polynomial scalar
  multiplication becomes multiplication by its image. The two quotients agree definitionally, so
  these equivalences isolate that identification cleanly.

Stated over arbitrary commutative rings.

## Provenance

The surjectivity argument — lift a class to a polynomial, then lift that polynomial along `f` — is
adapted from the AINTLIB `HasseWeil` project (`github.com/CBirkbeck/AINTLIB`, Apache-2.0, at
`dev/hasse-weil @ 513e83879e2f`),
`HasseWeil/WeilPairing/FrobeniusFunctionFieldEquiv.lean`, declaration `coordRingMap_bijective`.
There it is carried out for the coordinate ring of a Weierstrass curve and only for a base ring
*equivalence*; here it is stated for `AdjoinRoot.map` along any surjective base homomorphism, with
`map_mk` — which the source does not isolate — extracted as the step that makes it routine.
`AdjoinRoot.exists_degree_lt_mk_eq` and `AdjoinRoot.mk_eq_mk_iff_of_degree_lt` are adapted from
Michael Stoll's `EllipticCurves` project (`github.com/MichaelStollBayreuth/EllipticCurves`,
Apache-2.0, at commit `66889eada51a`),
`EllipticCurves/Mathlib/Basic.lean`. There the reduction step the first one uses is a separate
lemma; here that step is `AdjoinRoot.mk_modByMonic`. The source proves the second from a
named helper `eq_zero_of_monic_dvd_of_degree_lt`; here it follows directly from Mathlib's
`AdjoinRoot.mk_ne_zero_of_degree_lt`, so the helper is not re-declared, and `R` need not be
nontrivial. They are harvested here rather than in the file that consumes
them because nothing about elliptic curves enters either statement.
-/

public section

open Polynomial

namespace AdjoinRoot

variable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R]

section Map

variable [CommRing S]

/-- `AdjoinRoot.map` on the class of a polynomial is the class of its image. Mathlib states this
for `WeierstrassCurve.Affine.CoordinateRing.map` but not for the underlying `AdjoinRoot.map`. -/
@[simp]
lemma map_mk {f : R →+* S} {p : R[X]} {q : S[X]} (h : q ∣ p.map f) (x : R[X]) :
    map f p q h (mk p x) = mk q (x.map f) := by
  rw [map, lift_mk, ← Polynomial.eval₂_map]
  exact aeval_eq (x.map f)

/-- **`AdjoinRoot.map` is surjective when the base map is.** -/
lemma map_surjective {f : R →+* S} (hf : Function.Surjective f) {p : R[X]} {q : S[X]}
    (h : q ∣ p.map f) : Function.Surjective (map f p q h) := fun y => by
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective y
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := Polynomial.map_surjective f hf t
  exact ⟨mk p u, map_mk h u⟩

/-- The kernel of the quotient map `AdjoinRoot.mk p` is the ideal generated by `p`. -/
lemma ker_mk (p : R[X]) : RingHom.ker (mk p) = Ideal.span {p} :=
  Ideal.mk_ker

/-- Along a surjective base homomorphism `f`, the kernel of `AdjoinRoot p → AdjoinRoot (p.map f)`
is the extension of the kernel of `f`. -/
lemma ker_map_map_of_surjective {f : R →+* S} (hf : Function.Surjective f) (p : R[X]) :
    RingHom.ker (map f p (p.map f) dvd_rfl) = (RingHom.ker f).map (of p) := by
  have hcomp : (map f p (p.map f) dvd_rfl).comp (mk p) =
      (mk (p.map f)).comp (Polynomial.mapRingHom f) := by
    apply RingHom.ext
    intro x
    simp
  have hspan : (Ideal.span ({p} : Set R[X])).map (Polynomial.mapRingHom f) =
      Ideal.span {p.map f} := by simp [Ideal.map_span]
  have hcomap : (RingHom.ker (map f p (p.map f) dvd_rfl)).comap (mk p) =
      Ideal.span {p} ⊔ RingHom.ker (Polynomial.mapRingHom f) := by
    rw [RingHom.comap_ker, hcomp, ← RingHom.comap_ker, ker_mk, ← hspan,
      Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective _ (Polynomial.map_surjective f hf), RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot]
  rw [← Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective (mk p) mk_surjective
    (RingHom.ker (map f p (p.map f) dvd_rfl)), hcomap, Ideal.map_sup]
  have hzero : (Ideal.span ({p} : Set R[X])).map (mk p) = ⊥ := Ideal.map_quotient_self _
  rw [hzero, bot_sup_eq, Polynomial.ker_mapRingHom, Ideal.map_map, of]

/-- The reduction map `AdjoinRoot.algHomOfDvd` to the quotient by a divisor `g ∣ f` sends the class
of `p` modulo `f` to its class modulo `g`. -/
@[simp]
lemma algHomOfDvd_mk [Algebra R S] {f g : S[X]} (h : g ∣ f) (p : S[X]) :
    algHomOfDvd R f g h (mk f p) = mk g p := by
  simp [algHomOfDvd]

/-- Reducing modulo `g ∣ f` and then modulo `k ∣ g` is reducing modulo `k`. -/
@[simp]
lemma algHomOfDvd_algHomOfDvd [Algebra R S] {f g k : S[X]} (hgf : g ∣ f) (hkg : k ∣ g)
    (x : AdjoinRoot f) :
    algHomOfDvd R g k hkg (algHomOfDvd R f g hgf x) = algHomOfDvd R f k (hkg.trans hgf) x := by
  induction x using AdjoinRoot.induction_on with
  | ih p => simp only [algHomOfDvd_mk]

/-- `AdjoinRoot.algHomOfDvd_algHomOfDvd` as an equality of algebra maps. -/
@[simp]
lemma algHomOfDvd_comp_algHomOfDvd [Algebra R S] {f g k : S[X]} (hgf : g ∣ f) (hkg : k ∣ g) :
    (algHomOfDvd R g k hkg).comp (algHomOfDvd R f g hgf) = algHomOfDvd R f k (hkg.trans hgf) :=
  AlgHom.ext (algHomOfDvd_algHomOfDvd hgf hkg)

/-- Reducing modulo `f` itself is the identity. -/
@[simp]
lemma algHomOfDvd_self [Algebra R S] (f : S[X]) (h : f ∣ f) :
    algHomOfDvd R f f h = AlgHom.id R (AdjoinRoot f) :=
  AlgHom.ext fun x ↦ by
    induction x using AdjoinRoot.induction_on with
    | ih p => simp only [algHomOfDvd_mk, AlgHom.id_apply]

end Map

/-- An algebra map out of `AdjoinRoot g` sends the class of `p` to the evaluation of `p` at the
image of the root. -/
theorem algHom_mk {g : R[X]} {B F : Type*} [Semiring B] [Algebra R B] [FunLike F (AdjoinRoot g) B]
    [AlgHomClass F R (AdjoinRoot g) B] (φ : F) (p : R[X]) :
    φ (mk g p) = aeval (φ (root g)) p := by
  rw [← aeval_eq, aeval_algHom_apply]

section AlgHomEquiv

variable [Semiring S] [Algebra R S]

variable (S) in
/-- **Algebra maps out of `AdjoinRoot f` are the roots of `f`.** An `R`-algebra map
`AdjoinRoot f →ₐ[R] S` is determined by the image of the root, which can be any root of `f` in
`S`. The target need not be commutative, since `R` acts centrally on it. Mathlib's
`AdjoinRoot.equiv` is the version over a field with values in a domain, indexed by the multiset of
roots. -/
noncomputable def algHomEquiv (f : R[X]) :
    (AdjoinRoot f →ₐ[R] S) ≃ {x : S // aeval x f = 0} where
  toFun φ := ⟨φ (root f), by rw [← algHom_mk, mk_self, map_zero]⟩
  -- `AdjoinRoot.liftAlgHom` asks for a commutative target, so the inverse uses
  -- `Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ` instead.
  invFun x := Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _ (aeval x.val) fun p hp ↦ by
    obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hp
    rw [map_mul, x.property, mul_zero]
  left_inv φ := algHom_ext <| (Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk _ _ _).trans (aeval_X _)
  right_inv x := Subtype.ext <| (Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk _ _ _).trans (aeval_X _)

/-- The root of `f` attached to an algebra map out of `AdjoinRoot f` is the image of the root. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_algHomEquiv_apply {f : R[X]} (φ : AdjoinRoot f →ₐ[R] S) :
    (algHomEquiv S f φ : S) = φ (root f) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The algebra map out of `AdjoinRoot f` attached to a root `x` of `f` sends the root to `x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem algHomEquiv_symm_apply_root {f : R[X]} (x : {x : S // aeval x f = 0}) :
    (algHomEquiv S f).symm x (root f) = x :=
  congrArg Subtype.val ((algHomEquiv S f).apply_symm_apply x)

end AlgHomEquiv

/-- The class of `X` in `R[X]/(X ^ n - 1)` is an `n`th root of unity. -/
@[simp]
theorem root_X_pow_sub_one_pow (n : ℕ) : root (X ^ n - 1 : R[X]) ^ n = 1 := by
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← mk_X, ← map_pow, ← map_one (mk _), ← map_sub, mk_self]

/-- The class of `X` in `R[X]/(X ^ n - C a)` is an `n`th root of `a`. Mathlib's
`root_X_pow_sub_C_pow` is the same statement over a field. -/
@[simp]
protected theorem root_X_pow_sub_C_pow (n : ℕ) (a : R) : root (X ^ n - C a) ^ n = of _ a := by
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← eval₂_root, eval₂_sub, eval₂_C, eval₂_pow, eval₂_X]

/-- The class of `X` in `R[X]/(X ^ n - C a)` is a unit when `a` is a unit and `n ≠ 0`. -/
theorem isUnit_root_X_pow_sub_C {n : ℕ} {a : R} (ha : IsUnit a) (hn : n ≠ 0) :
    IsUnit (root (X ^ n - C a)) :=
  (isUnit_pow_iff hn).mp (by rw [AdjoinRoot.root_X_pow_sub_C_pow]; exact ha.map _)

/-- **The units of `AdjoinRoot f`.** The class of `g` is a unit of `AdjoinRoot f` exactly when
`f` and `g` are coprime, that is, when `g` is invertible modulo `f`. -/
@[simp]
theorem isUnit_mk_iff_isCoprime {f g : R[X]} : IsUnit (mk f g) ↔ IsCoprime f g :=
  -- `mk f` is by definition the quotient map `R[X] →+* R[X] ⧸ span {f}`, as in `mk_surjective`.
  Ideal.Quotient.isUnit_mk_iff.trans <| (Ideal.sup_eq_top_iff_isCoprime g f).trans isCoprime_comm

/-- For any `a, g ∈ R`, a power of `a` carries every element of `R[X] ⧸ (aX - g)` to a constant,
since `aX = g` there. -/
theorem exists_of_pow_mul_eq_of_C_mul_X_sub_C {a g : R} (x : AdjoinRoot (C a * X - C g)) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, ∃ r : R, AdjoinRoot.of _ (a ^ n) * x = AdjoinRoot.of _ r := by
  induction x using AdjoinRoot.induction_on with | ih f => ?_
  induction f using Polynomial.induction_on' with
  | add p q hp hq =>
    obtain ⟨m, r, hr⟩ := hp
    obtain ⟨n, s, hs⟩ := hq
    refine ⟨m + n, a ^ n * r + a ^ m * s, ?_⟩
    simp only [map_add, map_mul, map_pow] at hr hs ⊢
    linear_combination AdjoinRoot.of _ a ^ n * hr + AdjoinRoot.of _ a ^ m * hs
  | monomial k r =>
    refine ⟨k, r * g ^ k, ?_⟩
    have hroot : AdjoinRoot.of _ a * AdjoinRoot.root (C a * X - C g) = AdjoinRoot.of _ g := by
      have h := AdjoinRoot.mk_self (f := C a * X - C g)
      rwa [map_sub, map_mul, AdjoinRoot.mk_C, AdjoinRoot.mk_X, AdjoinRoot.mk_C, sub_eq_zero] at h
    rw [← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial]
    simp only [map_mul, map_pow, AdjoinRoot.mk_C, AdjoinRoot.mk_X]
    rw [← hroot]
    ring

/-- Modulo a product `p * q`, the class of the difference `p - q` is a unit exactly when `p` and
`q` are coprime. For a relator `p * (X - C x)` with a linear factor, `p - (X - C x)` is the
representative `C x - X + p`. -/
@[simp↓]
theorem isUnit_mk_mul_sub_iff_isCoprime {p q : R[X]} :
    IsUnit (mk (p * q) (p - q)) ↔ IsCoprime p q := by
  have h₁ : IsCoprime p (p - q) ↔ IsCoprime p q := by
    simpa using IsCoprime.mul_sub_left_right_iff (x := p) (y := q) (z := 1)
  have h₂ : IsCoprime q (p - q) ↔ IsCoprime p q := by
    simpa [isCoprime_comm (x := q)] using
      IsCoprime.sub_mul_left_right_iff (x := q) (y := p) (z := 1)
  simp [-map_sub, IsCoprime.mul_left_iff, h₁, h₂]

/-- For any relator `g`, the remainder `p %ₘ g` has the same class as `p` in
`AdjoinRoot g`. -/
@[simp]
lemma mk_modByMonic {g : R[X]} (p : R[X]) : mk g (p %ₘ g) = mk g p := by
  rw [Polynomial.modByMonic_eq_sub_mul_div, map_sub, map_mul, mk_self]
  simp

/-- **Every class in `AdjoinRoot g`, for `g` monic, is represented by a polynomial of degree
less than `deg g`.** Division with remainder by a monic polynomial supplies the representative. -/
lemma exists_degree_lt_mk_eq [Nontrivial R] {g : R[X]} (hg : g.Monic) (a : AdjoinRoot g) :
    ∃ p, p.degree < g.degree ∧ a = mk g p := by
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective a
  exact ⟨q %ₘ g, degree_modByMonic_lt q hg, by simp⟩

/-- **Two polynomials of degree less than that of a monic relator have the same class in
`AdjoinRoot` only if they are equal.** Together with `AdjoinRoot.exists_degree_lt_mk_eq` this says
that the polynomials of degree `< deg g` are a set of unique representatives. -/
lemma mk_eq_mk_iff_of_degree_lt {g : R[X]} (hg : g.Monic) {p q : R[X]}
    (hp : p.degree < g.degree) (hq : q.degree < g.degree) : mk g p = mk g q ↔ p = q :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ by_contra fun hne ↦ mk_ne_zero_of_degree_lt hg (sub_ne_zero.mpr hne)
      ((degree_sub_le p q).trans_lt (max_lt hp hq)) (by rw [map_sub, h, sub_self]),
    fun h ↦ h ▸ rfl⟩

/-- **An `R`-linear endomorphism of `AdjoinRoot g` commuting with multiplication by the root is
multiplication by its value at `1`.** It commutes with multiplication by every power of the root,
and these powers span `AdjoinRoot g`. -/
theorem eq_mulRight_of_root_mul {g : R[X]} {f : AdjoinRoot g →ₗ[R] AdjoinRoot g}
    (hf : ∀ x, f (root g * x) = root g * f x) :
    f = LinearMap.mulRight R (f 1) := by
  have hpow : ∀ i : ℕ, f (root g ^ i) = root g ^ i * f 1 := by
    intro i
    induction i with
    | zero => simp
    | succ i ih =>
      rw [pow_succ' (root g) i, hf, ih, ← mul_assoc, ← pow_succ' (root g) i]
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective x
  induction p using Polynomial.induction_on' with
  | add p q hp hq => simp only [map_add, hp, hq, LinearMap.mulRight_apply]
  | monomial n a =>
    rw [← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, map_mul, map_pow, mk_C, mk_X, ← algebraMap_eq,
      ← Algebra.smul_def, map_smul, hpow n, LinearMap.mulRight_apply, smul_mul_assoc]

/-- **The annihilator of `x ^ i` in `R[X]/(X ^ n)` is generated by `x ^ (n - i)`**, for `x` the
class of `X`: `x ^ i * c = 0` exactly when `x ^ (n - i)` divides `c`. Thus `x ^ i` and
`x ^ (n - i)` each generate the annihilator of the other. For `i > n` both sides hold, since then
`x ^ i = 0` and `n - i = 0`. -/
theorem root_X_pow_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff {n i : ℕ} (c : AdjoinRoot (X ^ n : R[X])) :
    root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ i * c = 0 ↔ root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ (n - i) ∣ c := by
  rcases le_or_gt i n with hi | hi
  · constructor
    · obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective c
      intro h
      rw [← mk_X, ← map_pow, ← map_mul, mk_eq_zero, ← pow_mul_pow_sub X hi] at h
      obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := h
      rw [mul_assoc] at hq
      obtain rfl := (isRegular_X_pow i).left hq
      exact ⟨mk _ q, by rw [map_mul, map_pow, mk_X]⟩
    · rintro ⟨d, rfl⟩
      rw [← mul_assoc, ← pow_add, Nat.add_sub_cancel' hi, ← mk_X, ← map_pow, mk_self, zero_mul]
  · have h0 : root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ i = 0 := by
      rw [← mk_X, ← map_pow, mk_eq_zero]
      exact pow_dvd_pow X hi.le
    simp [h0, Nat.sub_eq_zero_of_le hi.le]

/-- **The annihilator of `x ^ (n - i)` in `R[X]/(X ^ n)` is generated by `x ^ i`**, for `x` the
class of `X`: the companion of `AdjoinRoot.root_X_pow_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff` with the roles of `i`
and `n - i` exchanged. For `i > n` both sides say `c = 0`. -/
theorem root_X_pow_pow_sub_mul_eq_zero_iff {n i : ℕ} (c : AdjoinRoot (X ^ n : R[X])) :
    root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ (n - i) * c = 0 ↔ root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ i ∣ c := by
  rcases le_or_gt i n with hi | hi
  · simpa only [Nat.sub_sub_self hi] using root_X_pow_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff (i := n - i) c
  · have h0 : root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ i = 0 := by
      rw [← mk_X, ← map_pow, mk_eq_zero]
      exact pow_dvd_pow X hi.le
    simp [h0, Nat.sub_eq_zero_of_le hi.le]

/-- **The quotient of `R[X]/(X ^ n)` by `x ^ p` has rank `p`**, for `p ≤ n` and `x` the class of
`X`. This quotient is `R[X]/(X ^ p)`. -/
theorem finrank_quotient_span_root_X_pow_pow [Nontrivial R] {n p : ℕ} (hp : p ≤ n) :
    Module.finrank R (AdjoinRoot (X ^ n : R[X]) ⧸ Ideal.span {root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ p}) = p := by
  let φ := algHomOfDvd R (X ^ n : R[X]) (X ^ p) (pow_dvd_pow X hp)
  have hφ (q : R[X]) : φ (mk _ q) = mk _ q := by
    simp [φ, algHomOfDvd]
  have hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ p} := by
    ext c
    obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective c
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, hφ, mk_eq_zero, Ideal.mem_span_singleton, ← mk_X, ← map_pow]
    refine ⟨map_dvd _, fun ⟨d, hd⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective d
    rw [← map_mul, mk_eq_mk] at hd
    simpa using dvd_add ((pow_dvd_pow X hp).trans hd) (dvd_mul_right (X ^ p) r)
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective φ := by
    simp only [φ, algHomOfDvd, coe_mapAlgHom]
    exact map_surjective Function.surjective_id (by simpa using pow_dvd_pow X hp)
  rw [← (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R hker).toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq,
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hsurj).toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq,
    (powerBasis' (monic_X_pow p)).finrank, powerBasis'_dim, natDegree_X_pow]

open MulOpposite in
/-- **The quotient of the opposite of `R[X]/(X ^ n)` by `op (x ^ p)` has rank `p`**, for `p ≤ n`
and `x` the class of `X`. This is the form in which the quotient appears as a cyclic right
module over `R[X]/(X ^ n)`. -/
theorem finrank_quotient_span_op_root_X_pow_pow [Nontrivial R] {n p : ℕ} (hp : p ≤ n) :
    Module.finrank R ((AdjoinRoot (X ^ n : R[X]))ᵐᵒᵖ ⧸
      Ideal.span {op (root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ p)}) = p := by
  let e := Ideal.quotientEquivAlg (Ideal.span {root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ p})
    (Ideal.span {op (root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ p)}) (AlgEquiv.toOpposite R _)
    (by simp [Ideal.map_span])
  rw [← e.toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq, finrank_quotient_span_root_X_pow_pow hp]

open MulOpposite in
/-- **The quotient of `M_j` by the image of `x ^ m` has rank `min j m`**, where `M_j` is the
quotient of the opposite of `R[X]/(X ^ n)` by `op (x ^ j)`, for `j ≤ n` and `x` the class of `X`.
This quotient is `M_(min j m)`. -/
theorem finrank_quotient_map_mkQ_span_op_root_X_pow_pow [Nontrivial R] {n j : ℕ} (hj : j ≤ n)
    (m : ℕ) :
    Module.finrank R (((AdjoinRoot (X ^ n : R[X]))ᵐᵒᵖ ⧸
        Ideal.span {op (root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ j)}) ⧸
      (Submodule.map (Ideal.span {op (root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ j)}).mkQ
        (Ideal.span {op (root (X ^ n : R[X]) ^ m)})).restrictScalars R) = min j m := by
  rw [(Submodule.Quotient.restrictScalarsEquiv R _).finrank_eq,
    ((Submodule.quotientQuotientEquivQuotientSup _ _).restrictScalars R).finrank_eq, op_pow,
    op_pow, Ideal.span_singleton_pow_sup_span_singleton_pow, ← op_pow,
    finrank_quotient_span_op_root_X_pow_pow ((min_le_left j m).trans hj)]

section TensorProduct

open TensorProduct

variable (T : Type*) [CommRing T] [Algebra R T] (g : R[X])

/-- **Base change of `AdjoinRoot`.** For an `R`-algebra `T`, the base change of `R[X]/(g)` to `T`
is `T[X]/(g)`, with `g` mapped into `T[X]`; the class of `1 ⊗ X` goes to the class of `X`
(`algebraTensorAlgEquiv_one_tmul_root`). -/
noncomputable def algebraTensorAlgEquiv :
    T ⊗[R] AdjoinRoot g ≃ₐ[T] AdjoinRoot (g.map (algebraMap R T)) :=
  (tensorAlgEquiv g (g.map Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom) rfl).trans
    (mapAlgEquiv (Algebra.TensorProduct.rid R T T) _ _ (.of_eq (by
      rw [Polynomial.map_map]
      congr 1
      ext x
      simp [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one])))

/-- The base change of the root of `g` is the root of the image of `g` in `T[X]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem algebraTensorAlgEquiv_one_tmul_root :
    algebraTensorAlgEquiv T g (1 ⊗ₜ root g) = root (g.map (algebraMap R T)) := by
  rw [algebraTensorAlgEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply, tensorAlgEquiv_root, coe_mapAlgEquiv, map_root]

/-- The base change of the class of `p ∈ R[X]` is the class of the image of `p` in `T[X]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem algebraTensorAlgEquiv_one_tmul_mk (p : R[X]) :
    algebraTensorAlgEquiv T g (1 ⊗ₜ mk g p) =
      mk (g.map (algebraMap R T)) (p.map (algebraMap R T)) := by
  rw [← aeval_eq (p.map (algebraMap R T)), aeval_map_algebraMap]
  exact (algHom_mk (((algebraTensorAlgEquiv T g).toAlgHom.restrictScalars R).comp
    Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight) p).trans (by simp)

/-- The inverse of the base-change equivalence sends the root of the image of `g` in `T[X]` to the
base change of the root of `g`. -/
@[simp]
theorem algebraTensorAlgEquiv_symm_root :
    (algebraTensorAlgEquiv T g).symm (root (g.map (algebraMap R T))) = 1 ⊗ₜ root g := by
  rw [AlgEquiv.symm_apply_eq, algebraTensorAlgEquiv_one_tmul_root]

end TensorProduct

end AdjoinRoot

namespace AdjoinRoot

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The truncated polynomial algebra `R[X]/(X ^ N)` is free over `R`, with basis the powers of the
root below `N`. -/
instance free_X_pow (N : ℕ) : Module.Free R (AdjoinRoot (Polynomial.X ^ N : R[X])) :=
  (Polynomial.monic_X_pow N).free_adjoinRoot

/-- The truncated polynomial algebra `R[X]/(X ^ N)` is a finite `R`-module. -/
instance finite_X_pow (N : ℕ) : Module.Finite R (AdjoinRoot (Polynomial.X ^ N : R[X])) :=
  (Polynomial.monic_X_pow N).finite_adjoinRoot

section TensorProduct

open scoped TensorProduct

variable (k : Type*) [CommRing k] (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Algebra k R] (N : ℕ)

/-- **Base change of truncated polynomial algebras.** For a `k`-algebra `R`, the base change
`k[X]/(X ^ N) ⊗[k] R` is `R[X]/(X ^ N)`; it sends `root ⊗ 1` to the root and `1 ⊗ r` to `r`. -/
noncomputable def tensorXPowAlgEquiv :
    AdjoinRoot (Polynomial.X ^ N : k[X]) ⊗[k] R ≃ₐ[k] AdjoinRoot (Polynomial.X ^ N : R[X]) :=
  ((Algebra.TensorProduct.comm k _ R).trans
      ((algebraTensorAlgEquiv R (Polynomial.X ^ N : k[X])).restrictScalars k)).trans
    ((algEquivOfAssociated R _ (Polynomial.X ^ N : R[X]) (by simp)).restrictScalars k)

variable {k R N}

@[simp]
theorem tensorXPowAlgEquiv_root_tmul_one :
    tensorXPowAlgEquiv k R N (root (Polynomial.X ^ N : k[X]) ⊗ₜ 1) =
      root (Polynomial.X ^ N : R[X]) := by
  simp [tensorXPowAlgEquiv]

@[simp]
theorem tensorXPowAlgEquiv_one_tmul (r : R) :
    tensorXPowAlgEquiv k R N (1 ⊗ₜ r) = of (Polynomial.X ^ N : R[X]) r := by
  have h : r ⊗ₜ[k] (1 : AdjoinRoot (Polynomial.X ^ N : k[X])) = algebraMap R _ r := by
    rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply, Algebra.algebraMap_self, RingHom.id_apply]
  simp only [tensorXPowAlgEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.comm_tmul, h,
    AlgEquiv.restrictScalars_apply, AlgEquiv.commutes]
  rw [algebraMap_eq]

/-- `AdjoinRoot.tensorXPowAlgEquiv` is natural in the `k`-algebra `R`: base change along
`φ : R →ₐ[k] S` corresponds to the coefficientwise map `R[X]/(X ^ N) → S[X]/(X ^ N)`. -/
theorem tensorXPowAlgEquiv_comp_map {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] (φ : R →ₐ[k] S) :
    (tensorXPowAlgEquiv k S N).toAlgHom.comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id k _) φ) =
      (mapAlgHom φ (Polynomial.X ^ N) (Polynomial.X ^ N) (by simp)).comp
        (tensorXPowAlgEquiv k R N).toAlgHom := by
  ext <;> simp

end TensorProduct

end AdjoinRoot

namespace Polynomial

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The cyclic polynomial quotient, as an `R`-module, is `AdjoinRoot f`. -/
-- `AdjoinRoot f` is defined as `R[X] ⧸ Ideal.span {f}`, and `R[X] ∙ f` is that ideal, so the two
-- `R`-modules agree definitionally.
noncomputable def quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot (f : R[X]) :
    (R[X] ⧸ R[X] ∙ f) ≃ₗ[R] AdjoinRoot f :=
  LinearEquiv.refl R _

/-- The equivalence sends the class of a polynomial to its image in `AdjoinRoot`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot_mk (f g : R[X]) :
    quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot f (Ideal.Quotient.mk (R[X] ∙ f) g) = AdjoinRoot.mk f g := (rfl)

/-- Polynomial scalar multiplication on the cyclic quotient becomes multiplication
by the image of that polynomial in `AdjoinRoot`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot_smul (f g : R[X]) (y : R[X] ⧸ R[X] ∙ f) :
    quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot f (g • y) =
      AdjoinRoot.mk f g * quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot f y := by
  induction y using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
  | H h =>
    rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, smul_eq_mul, Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk, Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk,
      quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot_mk, quotientSpanEquivAdjoinRoot_mk, map_mul]

/-- The quotient `R[X] ⧸ Ideal.span {f}`, as an `R`-algebra, is `AdjoinRoot f`. -/
-- `AdjoinRoot f` is defined as `R[X] ⧸ Ideal.span {f}`, so the two `R`-algebras agree
-- definitionally; this isolates that unfolding in one place.
noncomputable def quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot (f : R[X]) :
    (R[X] ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) ≃ₐ[R] AdjoinRoot f :=
  AlgEquiv.refl

/-- `quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot` sends the class of a polynomial to its image in
`AdjoinRoot`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot_mk (f g : R[X]) :
    quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot f (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {f}) g) =
      AdjoinRoot.mk f g := (rfl)

/-- The inverse of `quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot` sends the image of a polynomial in `AdjoinRoot`
to its quotient class modulo `Ideal.span {f}`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot_symm_mk (f g : R[X]) :
    (quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot f).symm (AdjoinRoot.mk f g) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {f}) g := (rfl)

/-- The inverse of `quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot` sends `AdjoinRoot.root f` to the class of
`X`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot_symm_root (f : R[X]) :
    (quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot f).symm (AdjoinRoot.root f) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {f}) X := by
  rw [← AdjoinRoot.mk_X, quotientSpanAlgEquivAdjoinRoot_symm_mk]

end Polynomial

section IsWeaklyRegular

open RingTheory.Sequence

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {a g : R}

/-- **`a` stays regular on `R[X] ⧸ (aX - g)`.** If `a, g` is a weakly regular sequence on `R`, that
is, `a` is a nonzerodivisor on `R` and `g` is a nonzerodivisor on `R ⧸ (a)`, then multiplication
by `a` is injective on `R[X] ⧸ (aX - g)`. -/
theorem RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular.isSMulRegular_adjoinRoot_C_mul_X_sub_C
    (hag : IsWeaklyRegular R [a, g]) : IsSMulRegular (AdjoinRoot (C a * X - C g)) a := by
  obtain ⟨ha, hg⟩ := (isWeaklyRegular_cons_iff R a [g]).1 hag
  rw [isWeaklyRegular_singleton_iff, TauCeti.isSMulRegular_quotSMulTop_iff] at hg
  refine IsSMulRegular.of_right_eq_zero_of_smul fun x hx ↦ ?_
  induction x using AdjoinRoot.induction_on with | ih f => ?_
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, AdjoinRoot.algebraMap_eq, ← AdjoinRoot.mk_C, ← map_mul,
    AdjoinRoot.mk_eq_zero] at hx
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hx
  -- `g k = a (X k - f)`, so every coefficient of `k` is a multiple of `a`.
  have hgk : C a * (X * k - f) = C g * k := by
    linear_combination -hk
  have hka : k ∈ (Ideal.span {a}).map C := by
    refine Ideal.mem_map_C_iff.mpr fun n ↦ ?_
    have hn := congr_arg (fun p : R[X] ↦ p.coeff n) hgk
    simp only [coeff_C_mul] at hn
    obtain ⟨y, -, hy⟩ := (Submodule.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists _ _ _).1 (hg _ _ hn)
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mpr ⟨y, by rw [← hy, smul_eq_mul, mul_comm]⟩
  rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton] at hka
  obtain ⟨k', rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp hka
  -- Cancelling `a` in `a f = a ((aX - g) k')` gives `f = (aX - g) k'`.
  have hf : f = (C a * X - C g) * k' := ha.polynomial (by
    dsimp only
    rw [smul_eq_C_mul, smul_eq_C_mul, hk]
    ring)
  rw [hf, map_mul, AdjoinRoot.mk_self, zero_mul]

end IsWeaklyRegular

end
